  "body": "This PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Type | Update | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [eslint-import-resolver-webpack](https://togithub.com/benmosher/eslint-plugin-import) | devDependencies | minor | [`0.11.1` -> `0.12.0`](https://renovatebot.com/diffs/npm/eslint-import-resolver-webpack/0.11.1/0.12.0) |\n\n---\n\n### Release Notes\n\n<details>\n<summary>benmosher/eslint-plugin-import</summary>\n\n### [`v0.12.0`](https://togithub.com/benmosher/eslint-plugin-import/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md#&#8203;0120---2015-12-14)\n\n##### Changed\n\n-   Ignore [`import/ignore` setting] if exports are actually found in the parsed module. Does this to support use of `jsnext:main` in `node_modules` without the pain of managing an allow list or a nuanced deny list.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n### Renovate configuration\n\n:date: **Schedule**: \"every weekend\" in timezone Europe/Paris.\n\n:vertical_traffic_light: **Automerge**: Enabled.\n\n:recycle: **Rebasing**: Whenever PR is stale, or if you modify the PR title to begin with \"`rebase!`\".\n\n:no_bell: **Ignore**: Close this PR and you won't be reminded about this update again.\n\n---\n\n - [ ] <!-- rebase-check -->If you want to rebase/retry this PR, check this box\n\n---\n\nNewsflash: Renovate has joined WhiteSource, and is now free for all use. [Learn more](https://renovate.whitesourcesoftware.com/blog/renovate-is-now-part-of-whitesource/) or view updated [terms](https://renovate.whitesourcesoftware.com/terms-of-service/) and [privacy](https://renovate.whitesourcesoftware.com/privacy-policy/) policies.",
